 `repo doctor` answers in one shot why work is waiting, slow or failing when many agents share one worktree. It only reads state: it takes no lease and no capacity grant, so it answers even while a build holds everything; only the image repair of `--fix` tries one image lease once without waiting, so it never races a reclaim.
 
